;; Where projector's triage got to, per intake channel: the newest :event/at among the intake/
;; events system:projector wrote, one row per :intake/<channel> kind. An intake event happens when
;; the connector event it judged did, so a channel's connector events newer than this are the ones
;; it has not judged (src/intake/connectors.ts reads it as the cursor; nothing is stored in the
;; vault). No row for a channel never judged, which reads its window instead.
[:find ?kind (max ?at)
 :where
 (alias ?s "system:projector")
 (of-system ?e ?s)
 [?e :event/kind ?k]
 [(str ?k) ?kind]
 [(clojure.string/starts-with? ?kind ":intake/")]
 [?e :event/at ?at]]
